 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Homogeneous Regions:** Thresholding maps zero-difference vectors to the zero vector [S1, unofficial]. This is critical for maximizing codeword efficiency [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Precision:** Mean values are stored directly as 8-bit values [S1, unofficial]. Not given in the sources whether scaling or offsetting is required for wider ranges [G].
-*   **Boundary Conditions:** The volume dimensions $N_x, N_y, N_z$ must be divisible by 4 to partition into disjoint $4^3$ blocks [S1, unofficial]. If not, padding or partial block handling is required (not specified in sources) [G].
+*   **Homogeneous Regions:** Thresholding maps zero-difference vectors to the zero vector. This requires the codebooks to contain a zero vector or a vector very close to zero to efficiently represent these regions [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Precision:** Mean values are stored as 8-bit integers. This may introduce quantization error for the base level, which is then compounded by the difference vectors [S1, unofficial].
